# Nix artifacts
#
# The only tracked flake.lock is the root's, which belongs to this repo's own
# registry flake — no template ships one, and template-hygiene forbids it.
flake.lock
!/flake.lock

# devenv writes these into whatever directory it runs in, including a template
# directory a maintainer is debugging. .claude/hooks/git-add-before-nix.sh does
# not match a bare `devenv` command, so nothing is staged at that moment — but
# the next nix command in the session stages the whole working tree, and
# .devenv/ holds a live postgres data directory. The test-template skill tells
# you to go poke at a failing copy, so this is not hypothetical.
#
# devenv.lock is the template lock: ignored by default because templates ship
# unlocked (a consumer resolves current nixpkgs on first use), re-included per
# template with `!/templates/<name>/devenv.lock` when `locked = true` — the
# lock-policy check enforces that the two agree. CLAUDE.md 5.
devenv.lock
.devenv/
.devenv.flake.nix

result
result-*
.direnv/

.claude/settings.local.json
